[52.236072, "o", "    \u001b[0m\u001b[94mdef\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[90m \u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[92mtest_check_model_dir_size\u001b[39;49;00m():\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.236334, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.236574, "o", "        \u001b[90m# check if the model dir is smaller than 100KB\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.236778, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.237019, "o", "        model_dir = Path(\u001b[33m\"\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33m/app/trained_model\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33m\"\u001b[39;49;00m)\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.237216, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.237428, "o", "    \u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.237642, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.237861, "o", ">       total_size = subprocess.check_output(\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.238076, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.238312, "o", "            [\u001b[33m\"\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33mdu\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33m\"\u001b[39;49;00m, \u001b[33m\"\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33m-sb\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33m\"\u001b[39;49;00m, \u001b[96mstr\u001b[39;49;00m(model_dir)], text=\u001b[94mTrue\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.238531, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.238683, "o", "        ).split()[\u001b[94m0\u001b[39;49;00m]\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.238871, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.239104, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.239335, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[31m/tests/test_outputs.py\u001b[0m:22: "]
[52.239544, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.239809, "o", "_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ "]
[52.240035, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.240263, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[31m/usr/local/lib/python3.13/subprocess.py\u001b[0m:472: in check_output"]
[52.240458, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.241317, "o", "    \u001b[0m\u001b[94mreturn\u001b[39;49;00m run(*popenargs, stdout=PIPE, timeout=timeout, check=\u001b[94mTrue\u001b[39;49;00m,\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.241539, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.241736, "o", "_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ "]
[52.241925, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.242146, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.242407, "o", "input = None, capture_output = False, timeout = None, check = True, popenargs = (['du', '-sb', '/app/trained_model'],), kwargs = {'stdout': -1, 'text': True}"]
[52.242684, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.242898, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.250061, "o", "    \u001b[0m\u001b[94mdef\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[90m \u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[92mrun\u001b[39;49;00m(*popenargs,\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.250367, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.250607, "o", "            \u001b[96minput\u001b[39;49;00m=\u001b[94mNone\u001b[39;49;00m, capture_output=\u001b[94mFalse\u001b[39;49;00m, timeout=\u001b[94mNone\u001b[39;49;00m, check=\u001b[94mFalse\u001b[39;49;00m, **kwargs):\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.250812, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.251035, "o", "    \u001b[90m    \u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33m\"\"\"Run command with arguments and return a CompletedProcess instance.\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.252198, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.252425, "o", "    \u001b[33m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.252632, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.252834, "o", "    \u001b[33m    The returned instance will have attributes args, returncode, stdout and\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.253052, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.253259, "o", "    \u001b[33m    stderr. By default, stdout and stderr are not captured, and those attributes\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.253461, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.253692, "o", "    \u001b[33m    will be None. Pass stdout=PIPE and/or stderr=PIPE in order to capture them,\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.253877, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.254102, "o", "    \u001b[33m    or pass capture_output=True to capture both.\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.254293, "o", "\r\n"]
[52.254554, "o", "    \u001b[33m\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    If check is True and the exit code was non-zero, it raises a\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n"]
[52.25464, "o", "    \u001b[33m    CalledProcessError. The CalledProcessError object will have the return code\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    in the returncode attribute, and output & stderr attributes if those streams\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.254876, "o", "\r\n    \u001b[33m    were captured.\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    If timeout is given, and the process takes too long, a TimeoutExpired\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    exception will be raised.\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n"]
[52.255018, "o", "    \u001b[33m    There is an optional argument \"input\", allowing you to\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    pass bytes or a string to the subprocess's stdin.  If you use this argument\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    you may not also use the Popen constructor's \"stdin\" argument, as\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    it will be used internally.\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.255296, "o", "\r\n    \u001b[33m\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    By default, all communication is in bytes, and therefore any \"input\" should\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n"]
[52.255392, "o", "    \u001b[33m    be bytes, and the stdout and stderr will be bytes. If in text mode, any\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    \"input\" should be a string, and stdout and stderr will be strings decoded\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    according to locale encoding, or by \"encoding\" if set. Text mode is\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n"]
[52.255592, "o", "    \u001b[33m    triggered by setting any of text, encoding, errors or universal_newlines.\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n    \u001b[33m    The other arguments are the same as for the Popen constructor.\u001b[39;49;00m"]
[52.255615, "o", "\r\n    \u001b[33m    \"\"\"\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n        \u001b[94mif\u001b[39;49;00m \u001b[96minput\u001b[39;49;00m \u001b[95mis\u001b[39;49;00m \u001b[95mnot\u001b[39;49;00m \u001b[94mNone\u001b[39;49;00m:\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n"]
[52.255816, "o", "            \u001b[94mif\u001b[39;49;00m kwargs.get(\u001b[33m'\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33mstdin\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33m'\u001b[39;49;00m) \u001b[95mis\u001b[39;49;00m \u001b[95mnot\u001b[39;49;00m \u001b[94mNone\u001b[39;49;00m:\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m\r\n                \u001b[94mraise\u001b[39;49;00m \u001b[96mValueError\u001b[39;49;00m(\u001b[33m'\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33mstdin and input arguments may not both be used.\u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[33m'\u001b[39;49;00m)\u001b[90m\u001b[39;49;00m"]
